    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Detect voice-active segments in a local audio or video file (VAD).\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input audio or video file path.\r\n          --output TEXT       Optional: write the full VAD result JSON to this path.\r\n          --start TEXT        Start time, e.g. 0s / 500ms / 1200000us. Default 0s.\r\n          --end TEXT          End time. Mutually exclusive with --duration. Omit to scan to\r\n                              file end.\r\n          --duration TEXT     Duration. Mutually exclusive with --end.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media vad --input /tmp/speech.m4a\r\n  $ lyra-cli media vad --input /tmp/clip.mp4 --start 3s --duration 30s\r\n  $ lyra-cli media vad --input /tmp/talk.mp3 --output /tmp/vad.json\r\n\r\nTIME LITERALS\r\n  Time values accept `1.5s`, `500ms`, or `1200000us`.\r\n  --end and --duration are mutually exclusive; omit both to scan to file end.\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - Detection runs fully locally with JianYing Pro's aed40_10m model; no upload.\r\n  - Segment boundaries have approximately one-second resolution.\r\n  - Segments are half-open [start_us, start_us + duration_us) in microseconds.\r\n  - The model and detection policy are bundled with lyra-cli.\r\n  - It does not read or modify a draft.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Detect voice-active segments in a local audio or video file (VAD).\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input audio or video file path.\r\n          --output TEXT       Optional: write the full VAD result JSON to this path.\r\n          --start TEXT        Start time, e.g. 0s / 500ms / 1200000us. Default 0s.\r\n          --end TEXT          End time. Mutually exclusive with --duration. Omit to scan to\r\n                              file end.\r\n          --duration TEXT     Duration. Mutually exclusive with --end.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media vad --input /tmp/speech.m4a\r\n  $ lyra-cli media vad --input /tmp/clip.mp4 --start 3s --duration 30s\r\n  $ lyra-cli media vad --input /tmp/talk.mp3 --output /tmp/vad.json\r\n\r\nTIME LITERALS\r\n  Time values accept `1.5s`, `500ms`, or `1200000us`.\r\n  --end and --duration are mutually exclusive; omit both to scan to file end.\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - Detection runs fully locally with JianYing Pro's aed40_10m model; no upload.\r\n  - Segment boundaries have approximately one-second resolution.\r\n  - Segments are half-open [start_us, start_us + duration_us) in microseconds.\r\n  - The model and detection policy are bundled with lyra-cli.\r\n  - It does not read or modify a draft.\r\n",
